Added specification 2 of `repository.toml`, selected by a top-level `spec_version = "2"`. It replaces the `[backend]` and `[frontend]` component tables with a flat `[[package]]` array, where each entry declares a `type` (`python-plone`, `python`, `node-volto`, `node-aurora` or `node`) and optionally `primary = true`. A repository can now release several backend or frontend packages, and a single Python or Node package living at the repository root. Files without `spec_version` keep the specification 1 behavior. Both specifications are described by JSON Schemas shipped with repoplone, and `repoplone settings migrate` converts an existing file. @ericof
